<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gefco yr shr slips, cautions on div.</title>
<headline>Gefco yr shr slips, cautions on div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre excepts	   11.2	vs	15.3</p>
<p>- post excepts and</p>
<p>income appropriated for</p>
<p>expenditure on mining</p>
<p>    assets		    12.4	vs	8.3</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 9.0	 vs	9.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   4.47	vs	4.82</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   8.15	vs	4.59</p>
<p>    Tax			 3.69	vs	0.23 received</p>
<p>    Interest received     3.58	vs	5.45</p>
<p>    Turnover		  42.40     vs	48.37</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.20	vs	1.07</p>
<p>Div payable April 3</p>
<p>on register March 7</p>
<p>Full name: The Griqualand Exploration and Finace Company Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said a further reduction in sales tonnage of asbestos was expected during this year. It said information gathered pointed to a further decline of amphibole fibre points and production would be discontinued from end of March. It said the brick operation would continue to operate.</p>
<p>Dividend prospects should be viewed with caution taking note of the high costs of closing down the blue asbestos mining operation and with the brickworks not expected to make a significant contribution to group results, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
